Hi,
I am trying to convert a stan example to pymc3 which uses HMM. The log likelihood is calculated (using the forward algorithm) as follows:
    for (t in 2:N) {
        for (k in 1:K) {
            for (j in 1:K)
                acc[j] <- lg_alpha[t-1,j] + log(theta[j,k]) + normal_log(y[t],mu[k],sigma[k]);
            lg_alpha[t,k] <- log_sum_exp(acc);
        }
    }
    increment_log_prob(log_sum_exp(lg_alpha[N]));

I understand that I probably have to use DensityDist but I'm not too familiar with theano to write the above code efficiently. Could someone give me a starting point so that I could implement this? y[t] are the only obesrvations here.
My second question is that is there a way to ensure that mu[1]>mu[2]>mu[3]. This will avoid some of the problems of label switching and stan implements this with ordered variables.
